{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Dch5rrvob19Krv8d8NE6Yp", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lean_(proof_assistant)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2411.11885\"}, {\"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.09336v1\"}, {\"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.09336\"}, {\"url\": \"https://gwern.net/doc/www/arxiv.org/1a40b20044b5ee40e2857f8173dd799c4337ec47.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/4.20.0/Introduction/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://alphaxiv.org/abs/1910.09336\"}, {\"url\": \"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol299-fscd2024/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.3/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.3.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wiki.krisyotam.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic_2026-03/Lean_4\"}, {\"url\": \"https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/concept/62889984\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:06:38.516Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Lean mathlib history created 2017", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01P3SBx7QufaDECe3vBkUfSm", "content": [{"title": "Lean (proof assistant)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lean_(proof_assistant)"}, {"title": "Anatomy of a Formal Proof", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2411.11885"}, {"title": "arxiv.org", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.09336v1"}, {"title": "arxiv.org", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.09336"}, {"title": "gwern.net", "url": "https://gwern.net/doc/www/arxiv.org/1a40b20044b5ee40e2857f8173dd799c4337ec47.pdf"}, {"title": "The Lean Language Reference", "url": "https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/4.20.0/Introduction/"}, {"title": "The Lean mathematical library", "url": "https://alphaxiv.org/abs/1910.09336"}, {"title": "dagstuhl.de", "url": "https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol299-fscd2024/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.3/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.3.pdf"}, {"title": "Lean (proof assistant)", "url": "https://wiki.krisyotam.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic_2026-03/Lean_4"}, {"title": "graphsearch.epfl.ch", "url": "https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/concept/62889984"}]}, "Mathlib dates to 2017, when the community library began as a project to formalize pure mathematics in Lean.\n\n- **Origins:** In 2017, a community-maintained project to develop a Lean library mathlib began, with the goal to digitize as much of pure mathematics as possible in one large cohesive library.\n- **Code base:** In the summer of 2017, much of the core library for Lean was factored out of the system repository. This code became the base for mathlib.\n- **Early leadership:** The project was initially led by Mario Carneiro and Johannes Hölzl at Carnegie Mellon University.\n- **Version history:** January 20, 2017 saw the first release of the Lean 3.0 series. Mathlib was ported to Lean 4 in 2023, and it has now grown to over 1.5 million lines.\n- **Early activity:** One source notes that in total there have been a bit more than 30,000 contributions since Mathlib's inception in 2017."], "durationSeconds": 3.513190625, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Dch5rrvob19Krv8d8NE6Yp", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
